<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>💦 LIVE CONDENSATION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/condensation/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Condensation-favorability index 0-100 (DERIVED from HRRR analysis, fixed absolute scale): <b>0 No condensation</b> tan (dew-point depression at/above 2.5 C with RH at/below 60%) &rarr; <b>20 Relative humidity</b> gold &rarr; <b>40 Dew-point depression</b> green &rarr; <b>60 Dew-point depression</b> teal &rarr; <b>80 Surfaces stay wet</b> steel blue &rarr; <b>100 Saturation</b> deep blue (spread at/below 0 C with RH 100%). Relative humidity alone reaches 35; the depression term alone reaches 65; both together reach saturation. Same index always shows the same color — not relative humidity renamed, not dew point renamed, no fog visibility gate.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km 2 m TMP+DPT+RH analysis, hourly cycles (derived condensation-favorability index)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>💦 LIVE CONDENSATION — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Condensation.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>3600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
